pnpm lint-staged

# lint-staged only runs plain `oxlint`, which never loads tsgolint — so every
# type-aware rule is silently absent from the commit gate. Run them here, over
# the whole workspace rather than the staged files, because a type-aware rule
# needs the whole program to say anything.
#
# The library is built first: the docs site resolves `lekh-editor` through the types
# in dist/, and a stale or missing dist turns every import into an error type
# that the type-aware rules report as a fault in the docs site.
pnpm --filter lekh-editor build
pnpm lint:types
